  #line-at(38.835pt, 449.744pt, "across the (a) original, (b) attenuation-compensated, and (c) cross-compensated volumes, followed by the removal of")
  #line-at(38.835pt, 461.699pt, "isolated clusters smaller than 500 voxels to increase the emphasis on the dominant scattering regions for comparison.")
  #line-at(53.779pt, 473.655pt, "In the original data, the hotspot distributions from the two inspection faces show substantial separation along the")
  #line-at(38.835pt, 485.61pt, "depth direction, reflecting cumulative energy losses due to beam spreading and scattering. Conventional attenuation")
  #line-at(38.835pt, 497.565pt, "compensation reduces this discrepancy but only to a limited extent. Cross-directional compensation further improves")
  #line-at(38.835pt, 509.52pt, "the spatial alignment, with clusters from both directions exhibiting a higher degree of overlap throughout the inspection")
  #line-at(38.835pt, 521.475pt, "volume.")
  #line-at(53.779pt, 533.43pt, "To quantify the degree of spatial agreement, the overlap between the two hotspot volumes reconstructed from the")
  #line-at(38.835pt, 545.386pt, "opposing inspection directions was evaluated using the Dice coefficient [")
