  #set text(font: "STIXGeneral-Regular", size: 9.963pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(38.835pt, 63.821pt, "remain after compensation. These residuals are not treated as errors, but as direction-dependent backscatter features")
  #line-at(38.835pt, 75.776pt, "retained by the normalisation procedure after removal of the smooth propagation-related bias.")
  #line-at(53.779pt, 87.731pt, "A further limitation is that the compensated backscatter response is not calibrated directly against macrozone size,")
  #line-at(38.835pt, 99.686pt, "morphology, orientation, or spatial extent. The EBSD maps provide important microstructural context, but they are not")
  #line-at(38.835pt, 111.641pt, "registered volumetric measurements of the exact inspected region. Therefore, the residual fluctuations and volumetric")
  #line-at(38.835pt, 123.597pt, "hotspots are not interpreted as direct measurements or reconstructions of macrozone morphology. Instead, they are used")
  #line-at(38.835pt, 135.552pt, "in this study as signal-level indicators of spatial and directional backscatter consistency. A rigorous calibration of these")
  #line-at(38.835pt, 147.507pt, "features against the underlying macrozone field would require registered volumetric microstructure measurements or")
  #line-at(38.835pt, 159.462pt, "controlled numerical simulations in which the scattering distribution is known.")
